	)
	(text "AVDD33 x2, DVDD33, DVDD_RG: 100 nF each at the pin"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 232.41 334.01 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fdc7d8a5-a583-eee4-26c0-169e44201ed8")
	)
	(text_box "+3V3_ETH is +3V3 through a ferrite bead (power sheet).\nStraps pulled up through 4.7 k: RXD3 (PHYAD = 1), RXD1 (TXDLY = 1), RXD0 (RXDLY = 1). The PHY's internal\npull-ups would lose to the ECP5's pull-downs during configuration, when the straps are sampled:\nboth 2 ns RGMII delays inside the PHY, so the gateware adds none (LiteEth tx_delay = rx_delay = 0)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.2 335.28 0)
		(size 93.98 8.89)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7db2a0fa-3739-d8a3-4cae-9b827e07bd5f")
	)
	(text_box "The FPGA talks RGMII (4-bit DDR at 125 MHz) at 3.3 V to the PHY, through 22 Ω series resistors.\nThe PHY makes its own 1.0 V core with an internal switcher (REG_OUT, 2.2 µH).\nStraps on the LED and RXD pins are sampled at reset: CFG_EXT = 1 (external 3.3 V on DVDD_RG),\nCFG_LDO[1:0] = 00 (3.3 V I/O pads), PHY address 1, both RGMII delays inside the PHY (TXDLY = RXDLY = 1).\nThe magnetics are a G2406S module: each chip-side centre tap gets its own 100 nF to ground;\nthe line-side taps go to a Bob Smith termination (75 Ω each, 1 nF / 3 kV 1812 to ground)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 109.22 13.97)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fedb86bf-910e-ef94-be58-73e17360988b")
	)
